[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 986,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 951,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149915,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 951,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Inflammatory fibroid polyp is a benign, often polypoid, hypocellular fibroblastic neoplasm with a predilection for the stomach and ileum, containing a prominent inflammatory infiltrate, especially eosinophils.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 987,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 952,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149916,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 952,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>88256/0 Inflammatory fibroid polyp</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 988,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 953,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149917,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 953,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2E84.Y &amp; XA7MC7 Benign fibrogenic or myofibrogenic tumour of stomach</p>\r\n<p>2E84.Y &amp; XA0QT6 Benign fibrogenic or myofibrogenic tumour of ileum</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 989,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 954,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149918,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 954,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 990,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 955,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149919,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 955,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 991,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 956,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149920,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 956,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The stomach (especially the antrum) is the most commonly affected site, followed by the ileum, although inflammatory fibroid polyps may arise throughout the GI tract {721077;8214261}. Tumours are usually centred in the submucosa but can be restricted to the mucosa.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 992,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 957,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149921,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 957,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Tumours may be sessile or polypoid. Small upper GI tract tumours can be discovered incidentally at endoscopy. Larger tumours may present with abdominal pain, bleeding, or obstruction; half of patients with small intestinal tumours present with intussusception {23426127}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 993,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 958,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149922,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 958,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Inflammatory fibroid polyps are rare and represent &lt;&nbsp;0.1% of all gastric polypoid lesions. There is a slight female predominance and a peak incidence in middle-aged adults {20393746;32602395}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 994,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 959,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149923,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 959,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Most tumours are sporadic, but rare familial cases result from germline (constitutional) pathogenic variants in <em>PDGFRA</em>{6745724;25975287}. Pathogenic variant carriers often develop multiple tumours, including gastrointestinal stromal tumours {29486293}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 995,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 960,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149924,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 960,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>PDGFRA</em> activating mutations are identified in many cases, most often in small intestine tumours {18686281;19448595;20393746}; exon&nbsp;18 mutations, usually NM_006206.6:c.2525A&gt;T p.(Asp842Val), predominate in gastric tumours, whereas exon&nbsp;12 mutations are nearly always identified in small intestine tumours {22394371}. Germline <em>PDGFRA</em> mutations have been found in the rare familial cases {25975287}. Evolving data support that the lesional cells show telocyte differentiation; these CD34+/PDGFRA+ interstitial cells appear to be involved in neurotransmission {29486293;29981768;30117724}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1002,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 967,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149925,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 967,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Inflammatory fibroid polyps may be sessile or polypoid. Tumours range widely in size; gastric tumours are usually &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;mm, whereas ileal tumours are often larger. The cut surface is white and often fleshy.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 996,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 961,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149926,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 961,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Histological features include a poorly marginated, hypocellular lesion containing a haphazard arrangement of short spindled and stellate cells with fine chromatin, small or indistinct nucleoli, and scant eosinophilic cytoplasm. The stroma is often oedematous and sometimes myxoid or collagenous, with a prominent mixed inflammatory infiltrate, often rich in eosinophils and lymphocytes. Small and intermediate-sized, rounded blood vessels, some with concentric (onion-skin) fibrosis, are a typical finding.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, CD34 and PDGFRA are positive in most cases {9160309;19448595}. More limited SMA expression is observed in a small subset of tumours. KIT, DOG1 (ANO1), desmin, S100, SOX10, and keratins are negative.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 997,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 962,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149927,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 962,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 998,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 963,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149928,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 963,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1001,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 966,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149929,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 966,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a hypocellular appearance, with short spindled to stellate cells in an oedematous or myxoid stroma; an inflammatory infiltrate of eosinophils and lymphocytes.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> expression of CD34.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 999,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 964,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149930,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 964,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1000,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 965,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149931,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 965,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Inflammatory fibroid polyps are benign.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
